  "id": "h5",
  "order": 5,
  "title": "Finger independence",
  "summary": "Train the weak fingers, 4 and 5, to move on their own.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Finger independence",
      "body": "**Finger independence**: moving one finger while the others stay still and relaxed.\n\nFingers 4 and 5 are the weakest for everyone, because the ring finger shares its tendons with its neighbours. They get stronger with short, slow practice, a few minutes a day.\n\n**Why it matters:** independent fingers play a melody evenly, every note the same loudness, and keep one note from smearing into the next.",
      "hands": [
        {
          "hand": "right",
          "keys": [
            60,
            62,
            64,
            65,
            67
          ]
        }
      ],
